    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d597-a4">

                <pb facs="0710" n="636" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav01/pg636"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Appendix 3—Telegram—Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Soviet Commissar of Ways of Communication</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Zaikin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Station
                        Master at Vologda </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content"
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-23"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Undated</hi></date>.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d597-f1"/>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In accordance with an order from the People’s Commissar for Foreign Affairs
                    Chicherin, I request information without delay as to who from the American
                    Embassy and for what purpose is demanding a special train to Archangel. Until
                    the receipt of this information and the receipt by you of a permit to dispatch
                    the train, same should not be dispatched.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Zaikin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d597-f1" n="1" xml:id="d597-f1-content">
                <p>Received by the Vologda station master July 23, in the afternoon.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
